{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nm=json.load(open('map.json'));m['version']=7\nb14=[b for b in m['behaviors'] if b['id']=='B14-ballot-monotonicity'][0]\nb14['unknowns']=[\\\"resolved to a sourced relationship: the master designates a leader at registration (the configured Leader alias, or the replica with the lowest ping RTT when no Leader is configured) and calls Replica.BeTheLeader on it, and it promotes another replica through the same call when its ping loop finds the leader dead, so IsLeader is set from outside the epaxos package; whether a promoted replica's raised ballots interact with recovery in ways the checks have not covered stays open\\\"]\nb14.setdefault('important_branches',[]).append(\\\"IsLeader is set by the master's Replica.BeTheLeader call: during master startup for the replica it marked as leader, and again when its ping loop finds that leader dead and promotes the next candidate (S31-master-startup, S32-master-register)\\\")\njson.dump(m,open('map.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nsrcs=[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S31-master-startup\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"master/master.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":75,\\\"end_line\\\":190,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"S32-master-register\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"master/master.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":193,\\\"end_line\\\":260,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}]\nfb={\\\"ref_ids\\\":[\\\"B14-ballot-monotonicity\\\",\\\"S31-master-startup\\\",\\\"S32-master-register\\\",\\\"S24-runReplica-epaxos\\\",\\\"S5-broadcasters\\\"],\n \\\"answered\\\":\\\"B14's unknown about what sets IsLeader is answered: the master owns that flag. At registration it marks one replica as leader - the alias named by the config's Leader field, or, when no Leader is configured, the replica with the lowest ping RTT measured by the master's ping command - and reports IsLeader to it; during master startup and again whenever its ping loop finds a leader dead, it calls Replica.BeTheLeader on the marked replica via HTTP RPC (S31-master-startup, S32-master-register). For this target that call lands in epaxos.Replica.BeTheLeader, which sets IsLeader = true and returns nil, so the master's leader/nextLeader fields stay at their defaults and the promoting replica keeps the designation. IsLeader then feeds makeBallot, which raises the ballot above maxRecvBallot while the flag is set, so a promoted replica can out-ballot anything it has seen when it recovers an instance.\\\",\n \\\"remaining\\\":[\\\"whether the launched configuration sets a Leader alias at all, which decides between the configured designation and the lowest-ping-RTT choice (aws.conf was not read)\\\",\n   \\\"whether IsLeader = true changes the confirmed recovery finding: raising the ballot further leaves the self entry's VBallot equal to the new ballot, so the masking mechanism should persist, but no check has been run with the flag set\\\",\n   \\\"the open scope-issue bookkeeping on the superseded C1 artifact and the unread helper surfaces (replica/sender.go, replica/mset.go, hook/)\\\"],\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The master was the last protocol-relevant surface surfaced as deferred, and reading it resolves a map unknown with two new sources while keeping the ownership statement of the map (no global leader in the protocol) intact: the master's leader flag is a deployment notion that feeds the replica's ballot behaviour, which is why it belongs to B14's description rather than to the protocol's ownership list.\\\",\n \\\"understanding\\\":\\\"updated\\\",\\\"question_updates\\\":{}}\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"research\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Answers the ballot-monotonicity unknown with the master as the in-repository caller of Replica.BeTheLeader, and records that relationship in the map (B14) with two new sources. No requirement, binding, edge or identity changes; the read also notes that a promoted replica's raised ballots have not been exercised by any check, which stays as a remaining question rather than being folded into the confirmed finding.\\\",\n \\\"sources\\\":srcs,\\\"map_path\\\":\\\"map.json\\\",\n \\\"map_changes\\\":{\\\"B14-ballot-monotonicity\\\":{\\\"impact\\\":\\\"clarification\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The unknown about what sets IsLeader is replaced by the sourced relationship (master designation at registration and promotion on leader failure), and a branch records the two master call sites.\\\",\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S31-master-startup\\\",\\\"S32-master-register\\\",\\\"S5-broadcasters\\\"],\\\"preserves\\\":\\\"The ballot arithmetic, the nack-driven prepare path and the ownership statement of the target profile are unchanged; only the description of who sets the deployment leader flag is added.\\\"}},\n \\\"feedback\\\":fb}\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-master-b14.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('ok')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-master-b14.json 2>&1 | head -10\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
